<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="132ui" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Invoice Review notify step: see, edit and confirm the 131 notice before Reject / Return</title>
    <phase>5 Firm feedback (WP5)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <tags>frontend, react, fluent-ui, code-page, ebilling</tags>
    <dependencies>132 (on master fe51619cfc), 131 (Action seeded on dev 2026-11-19)</dependencies>
    <source>EB-D-258 (notes/decisions-log.md); notes/132-ebilling-notifications.md (owner question 2: "confirm 132ui covers both routes")</source>
  </metadata>

  <goal>
    On an In Review invoice, a reviewer who chooses Reject or Return to firm in the decision wizard sees the drafted notice to the firm,
    may edit its subject and prose, and sends it with the decision. The server already does everything else (132): it screens the
    confirmed notice before deciding, sends the email only when the request carries the notice, and stores the sent text. This task is
    client-only (src/solutions/InvoiceReview); no server, schema or shared-library change.
  </goal>

  <server-contract>
    <item>Draft: POST /api/finance/invoices/{invoiceId}/firm-notice/draft?kind=InvoiceRejected|ReturnedToFirm (no body). 200 FirmNoticeDraftResponse
      { kind, subject, prose, html, source ("Action" | "Template"), actionVersion, fallbackReason }. 400 ebilling.firm-notice.invalid_kind;
      404 uniform; 409 ebilling.firm-notice.not_applicable; 429 (rate limit "ai-batch", 20 per minute per user); 503 ebilling.disabled or
      ebilling.firm-notice.unavailable. Nothing is stored or sent. Source: Api/Finance/FirmNoticeEndpoints.cs.</item>
    <item>Decide: POST .../reject and .../return take InvoiceDecisionRequest { reason, note?, noticeSubject?, noticeProse? }
      (Api/Finance/InvoiceRejectReturnEndpoints.cs:168). When either notice part is non-blank the server screens both BEFORE deciding
      (FirmNoticeProse.ScreenConfirmed): a refusal is 400 ebilling.notice_refused with the reason code in the detail, and nothing is decided.
      With neither part, the decision stands and no firm email is sent (feed and status only).</item>
    <item>Limits (Services/Finance/FirmNoticeComposer.cs, FirmNoticeProse): subject 120 characters after the code-written tracking suffix is
      removed (the route accepts up to 280 with the suffix); prose 1500 characters. The prose may not contain digits, currency, links, number
      words or numbered line references; the table, amounts and clause quotes are added by code, never typed.</item>
  </server-contract>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step n="1">Replace the empty notifyStep slot with a built-in Notify step in components/decision (steps.tsx or a new NotifyStep file),
      shown on the Reject and Return paths when the wizard is editable (not on Approve, not read-only). Remove the slot prop chain
      (InvoiceReviewWithDecisions → DecideInvoiceAction → InvoiceDecisionWizard) if nothing else uses it, and replace the slot test
      (InvoiceDecisions.test.tsx "shows a supplied notify step…") with tests of the built-in step.</step>
    <step n="2">The step fetches the draft for the chosen outcome (reject → InvoiceRejected, return → ReturnedToFirm) when it is first shown,
      once per kind per opened wizard; switching outcome keeps each kind's draft and edits apart. Add the draft call to services/decisionApi.ts
      (same authenticatedFetch / ApiResult pattern as the other calls).</step>
    <step n="3">Show: an editable Subject field and an editable Message field (prose) with n / limit counters; a line saying where the text came
      from (AI draft, or the standard wording when the AI was unavailable); a short note that the findings table, amounts and clause quotes are
      added by Spaarke and are not editable; a "Restore draft" action. The HTML preview, if shown, is rendered only in a sandboxed iframe
      (srcdoc, sandbox with no allowances), never with dangerouslySetInnerHTML, and is labelled as the drafted version (edits are not reflected).</step>
    <step n="4">Sending is explicit: the step has a "Send this notice to the firm" choice, on by default once a draft loaded. Skip, or turning it
      off, sends the decision without a notice; the Confirm step then says plainly that the firm gets no email. A blank subject or prose with
      sending on blocks Next with a field message. A draft that failed to load (any non-200) shows the server's message and code, offers Retry,
      and lets the reviewer continue without a notice (never blocks the decision).</step>
    <step n="5">Pass noticeSubject and noticeProse (trimmed) with reject / returnToFirm when sending is on. A 400 ebilling.notice_refused is shown
      under the notice fields (like isNoteRefusal for the note), the wizard returns to or stays reachable at the Notify step, and nothing else
      changes. A decision that came back unsure locks the notice with the reason and note (decisionLocks / locks.set('wizard', …) must carry the
      notice and the send choice) so the repeat is the same request.</step>
    <step n="6">Tests in src/__tests__ (existing InvoiceDecisions.test.tsx patterns, mockDecisionApi): one per acceptance criterion below,
      including the negative ones. Run the package's tests, tsc and client-lint for the touched files.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion id="AC1">Reject and Return each show the Notify step after Reason; Approve and a read-only (decided) wizard never show it.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC2">The draft is requested with the kind matching the outcome, at most once per kind per opened wizard (no request on Approve,
      none before the step is shown); edits to one kind survive switching outcome and back.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC3">With sending on, the reject / return request carries exactly the edited, trimmed subject and prose; with sending off or the
      step skipped, it carries neither field (no empty strings).</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC4">The Confirm step states whether the firm will be emailed this notice or gets no email.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC5">A 400 ebilling.notice_refused shows the refusal under the notice fields; the decision is not shown as made; the reviewer can
      edit and finish again.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC6">A failed draft (409, 429, 503, network) shows the message and code with Retry, and the reviewer can still finish without a
      notice; nothing is sent with a half-loaded draft.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC7">Subject over 120 or prose over 1500 characters, or blank with sending on, holds Next with a field message; nothing is cut off
      silently.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC8">A decision that came back unsure reopens with the same reason, note, notice and send choice, locked.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC9">No dangerouslySetInnerHTML anywhere in the change; any preview uses a sandboxed iframe with no allowances.</criterion>
    <criterion id="AC10">Existing decision-wizard tests still pass; tsc and client-lint clean for touched files.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Nothing is computed or decided client-side; the server screens and decides. The client limits are hints that
      mirror the server's caps; the server stays the authority.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent UI v9 only, semantic tokens, dark mode.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Calls go through the existing authenticated decision API client; no raw fetch with headers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050 / D-58">The step lives in the existing WizardShell; no new modal.</constraint>
    <constraint>Do not change the server, the shared library (@spaarke/ui-components) or the external SPA.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <out-of-scope>
    <item>Showing the sent notice on a decided invoice (read-only wizard, History tab): the internal view is not asked for; the firm view is 130g.</item>
    <item>System rejections (SubmissionRejected) and Approved with adjustments: the server sends the composed draft unchanged (EB-D-258).</item>
    <item>The blocked-submission Override / Return (FormModal) path: no notice in R1.</item>
    <item>Deploying the page to dev: a separate step with the owner's OK (code-page-deploy).</item>
  </out-of-scope>

